# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Terraform (infra/terraform) — .terraform/ is a regenerated local cache of
# downloaded provider binaries (hundreds of MB, architecture-specific);
# never commit it. .terraform.lock.hcl (the version pin) is committed
# deliberately, unlike the directory above. terraform.tfstate is committed
# deliberately too (see infra/terraform/environments/dev/main.tf) — this is
# a single-operator sandbox account with no remote state backend yet — but
# its noisy .backup copy and crash logs never need to be.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
